# Fixture: the HC_PRE A/B card at 5 rounds (the band +0.9..+1.3): passes at 5, refused at 3 and 4.
kind: ab
question: does moving the attention sub-layer's ds41_hc_pre onto a branch stream inside the
  captured step shorten the V4.1 decode step?
term: decode tok/s @ n=96, lcg depth 6, A6000, plan (a) — (branch − base) / base, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +0.9..+1.3
rounds: 5
condition: the base and branch generate_ds41 binaries alternate in one lease
  (BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=5 just depth-gpu-ds41 6 bin:<base tree>/target/release/generate_ds41:6),
  the order rotated every round; no row carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
decide-in: land ds41hcbranch as it is
decide-below: keep the change out of the default and find the wrong term (contention, the join's
  cost) in an nsys timeline before another A/B
decide-above: land it and re-derive the join and contention terms the model overstated
